      info: "Public copy. Clones via `_copy()`, then — unless this shape is `tmp()` — adds the clone to the active layer. `copy()` means \"give me a new shape\", and new shapes render: the clone is attached whenever a layer is reachable, which includes copying a DETACHED but scene-derived shape (`curve.segments().first().copy()`) via the carried `_scene`. The clone inherits the opaque `_modeler` and is flagged `_nameInherited` so the host auto-namer can rename it after its variable.\n\nInside kernel operations use `_copy()` instead — it is the pure clone and never touches the scene. Do NOT reach for `tmp()` there: `_suppressScene` is sticky and propagates to every derived shape, so a tmp'd internal copy would suppress the real result too.",
